01028.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101028.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"As a side effect, `_replacement_char` has to be exposed (which makes sense because `0xfffd` is the official Unicode designated [replacement character](https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/U+FFFD)), and `print_unicode_error` has to be made static (which makes sense because it doesn't use any local string properties).\r\n\r\nThere is one final re-interpretation of characters in the `utf16` implementation, but this one needs to perform the checks anyway for different reasons.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, all callers now pass `p_critical=true`, which prints \"some characters were replaced with � (U+FFFD)\" so it was intended for this specific purpose. This used to not be the case for some of the callers, which I think is incorrect.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101028/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101028/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}